{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WN6rygA48RZctzA6ddMnaE","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd051-pwd\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/pwd: Print Working Directory\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Scripts use pwd to obtain the current working directory as an absolute path. The utility\n6\t  supports two modes: logical (-L, uses the PWD environment variable preserving symlink\n7\t  names) and physical (-P, resolves symlinks via the filesystem). The Go implementation\n8\t  must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gpwd, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte\n9\t  on stdout and exit code, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Print the absolute pathname of the current working directory.\n13\t  - G2: Support logical (-L) and physical (-P) modes.\n14\t\n15\trequirements:\n16\t  R1:\n17\t    title: Default behavior and modes\n18\t    items:\n19\t      - R1.1:\n20\t          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print the current working directory followed by a newline and exit 0. The default mode is -P (physical).\n21\t      - R1.2:\n22\t          text: \"-L (--logical) must print the value of the PWD environment variable if it names the current directory and contains no . or .. components. If PWD is unset or invalid, must fall back to physical mode.\"\n23\t      - R1.3:\n24\t          text: \"-P (--physical) must print the resolved physical path with all symlinks resolved.\"\n25\t      - R1.4:\n26\t          text: When both -L and -P are given, the last one specified takes precedence.\n27\t\n28\t  R2:\n29\t    title: Error handling\n30\t    items:\n31\t      - R2.1:\n32\t          text: If any positional operand is provided, must print an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n33\t      - R2.2:\n34\t          text: Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n35\t\n36\t  R3:\n37\t    title: Differential testing\n38\t    items:\n39\t      - R3.1:\n40\t          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (gpwd) via pkg/testutils.\n41\t      - R3.2:\n42\t          text: \"Tests must cover: default invocation, -L, -P, -L -P precedence, and error cases.\"\n43\t      - R3.3:\n44\t          text: All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment.\n45\t\n46\tnon_goals:\n47\t  - cmd/pwd does not change the working directory.\n48\t  - cmd/pwd does not support any output formatting options.\n49\t\n50\tacceptance_criteria:\n51\t  - id: AC1\n52\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/pwd prints the current directory, matching gpwd.\"\n53\t    traces:\n54\t      - R1.1\n55\t      - R1.2\n56\t      - R1.3\n57\t      - R1.4\n58\t  - id: AC2\n59\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/pwd -L prints the logical path from PWD, matching gpwd -L.\"\n60\t    traces:\n61\t      - R1.2\n62\t      - R1.4\n63\t      - R3.2\n64\t  - id: AC3\n65\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/pwd -P prints the physical path, matching gpwd -P.\"\n66\t    traces:\n67\t      - R1.1\n68\t      - R1.3\n69\t      - R1.4\n70\t      - R3.2\n71\t  - id: AC4\n72\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gpwd passes for all modes and error cases.\"\n73\t    traces:\n74\t      - R2.1\n75\t      - R2.2\n76\t      - R3.1\n77\t      - R3.2\n78\t      - R3.3\n79\t  - id: AC5\n80\t    criterion: \"cmd/pwd compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n81\t    traces:\n82\t      - R1.1\n83\t      - R1.2\n84\t      - R1.3\n85\t      - R1.4\n86\t      - R2.1\n87\t      - R2.2\n88\t      - R3.1\n89\t      - R3.2\n90\t      - R3.3\n91\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d635ec6d-b4f9-46ea-b855-65b46977b674","uuid":"34b4996e-1091-40c1-9a9e-1c418bd702cf","timestamp":"2026-05-15T00:18:48.631Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5231/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd051-pwd.yaml","content":"id: srd051-pwd\ntitle: \"cmd/pwd: Print Working Directory\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Scripts use pwd to obtain the current working directory as an absolute path. The utility\n  supports two modes: logical (-L, uses the PWD environment variable preserving symlink\n  names) and physical (-P, resolves symlinks via the filesystem). The Go implementation\n  must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gpwd, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte\n  on stdout and exit code, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Print the absolute pathname of the current working directory.\n  - G2: Support logical (-L) and physical (-P) modes.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default behavior and modes\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print the current working directory followed by a newline and exit 0. The default mode is -P (physical).\n      - R1.2:\n          text: \"-L (--logical) must print the value of the PWD environment variable if it names the current directory and contains no . or .. components. If PWD is unset or invalid, must fall back to physical mode.\"\n      - R1.3:\n          text: \"-P (--physical) must print the resolved physical path with all symlinks resolved.\"\n      - R1.4:\n          text: When both -L and -P are given, the last one specified takes precedence.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Error handling\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: If any positional operand is provided, must print an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Differential testing\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (gpwd) via pkg/testutils.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: default invocation, -L, -P, -L -P precedence, and error cases.\"\n      - R3.3:\n          text: All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/pwd does not change the working directory.\n  - cmd/pwd does not support any output formatting options.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/pwd prints the current directory, matching gpwd.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/pwd -L prints the logical path from PWD, matching gpwd -L.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.4\n      - R3.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/pwd -P prints the physical path, matching gpwd -P.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R3.2\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gpwd passes for all modes and error cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"cmd/pwd compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n","numLines":91,"startLine":1,"totalLines":91}}}
