{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01MkvK1DkUM2UkK1o5sJwT2X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! The GNU `gpwd` reference binary actually ignores extra operands — it prints a warning to stderr (\"pwd: ignoring non-option arguments\") but still prints the working directory and exits 0. Our Go implementation treats them as errors (exit 1).\n\nThe SRD says R2.1: \"If any positional operand is provided, must print an error message to stderr and exit 1.\" But the differential test shows that the reference binary (gpwd) does NOT exit 1 for extra operands — it ignores them with a warning and exits 0.\n\nSince the differential testing requirement (R3.1) says we must match the reference binary, and R2.1 says we should error on extra operands, there's a conflict. \n\nThe real tension is that R2.1 demands an error exit, but gpwd actually warns and continues with exit 0 — so I need to decide whether to follow the specification literally or match the reference binary's actual behavior, since both R2.1 and R3.1 are requirements. Updating the Go implementation to handle the `--` case...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1046,"cache_read_input_tokens":31339,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1046},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d635ec6d-b4f9-46ea-b855-65b46977b674","uuid":"3cf38c27-7a68-4a98-b9c5-4231b28f330d"}
